      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Stenoses in branch vessels which originate at acute angle to the main vessel represent a technically challenging anatomy for the performance of balloon angioplasty [PTCA]. We report a novel technique utilizing a distally placed perfusion balloon that facilitated guidewire placement and subsequent balloon angioplasty of a branch vessel stenosis."},
